1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
How does AI learn? It rolls downhill. One line of maths, a few billion times.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,600
This curve is how WRONG the model is.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,000
The bottom of the valley is the right answer.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,400
The model starts up here, and it cannot see where the bottom is.

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,600
Where is it now? Four.

6
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,800
Which way is downhill? The slope where you stand. Along 1, up 2 — the slope is 2.

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:18,400
The step is the one number you choose. Call it 1.

8
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:22,400
Four, minus one times two, is two. The ball moved downhill.

9
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,600
The new one becomes the old one.

10
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:29,600
Now do it again. Two minus one times one is one. Smaller slope, smaller step.

11
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,800
Flat ground. Nothing left to change. That is training — a few billion times.

12
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,400
We learned this at school. Nobody ever said what for.

13
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:40,000
Pause. Observe. Learn. Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
